      "writtenOn": "2022-11-24T16:50:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I\u0027ve noticed that. I can see how that would be hard to debug but not a blocker - you can always keep a thread around.\n\nI\u0027m in two minds about this. If we used a pipe FD instead, thread ID would not be a problem and feels cleaner as well. On the other hand, an app can probably pass its FD to someone else to keep it alive beyond its own death. I guess that\u0027s okay since it\u0027s still the app UID process? Would the child process even get reaped?",
      "parentUuid": "3bca5f46_d89eba2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 57
